Historical PHY model, test-only
===============================

legacy_model.rs was moved out of net/sparklink/sle_phy.rs for R09 cleanup.
It contains the old local MCS/MIMO/default PHY/parameter encoder model. These
tables and codecs have not been qualified against the current standard/WS73
firmware, and are not reference vectors or a supported hardware interface.

run_phy_model.py compiles this isolated model and the unchanged production
channel-map/hopping helpers with dependency fixtures under -D warnings. The
three tests retain local boundary/roundtrip/history coverage, without global
dead_code suppression or a second copy of production channel-map algorithms.
The actual unsupported PHY match arm is compiled separately, with only its
constant identifiers and kernel Error constructor supplied by fixtures.

These are development checks, not VFS, hardware completion, security, AFH
standard conformance, lockdep or RF acceptance. The production PHY observation,
setter, local selection/hopping/SINR ioctls return EOPNOTSUPP. The legacy
adapter-global encryption enable rejects even artificially pre-populated
Paired keys; future authenticated per-connection installation/completion is
still required. No defaults or local estimates are reported as hardware state.

ChannelMap/HoppingState remain in the legacy connection path pending the
connection/socket migration; their presence does not qualify link/PHY support.
